Honor libinput's per-device WL_OUTPUT mapping for identical touch controllers.

Linux's RG DS has two Goodix touch devices with the same vendor, product and
name. libinput's udev backend already reads the established WL_OUTPUT property:
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/libinput/libinput/-/blob/1.31.3/src/udev-seat.c#L139
Expose that name through wlr_touch.output_name so Sway's existing default
mapping uses it. The returned libinput string is borrowed; wlr_touch_finish
owns and frees its copy. Without WL_OUTPUT this is a no-op.

Upstream review (2026-10-25): wlroots MR searches for
libinput_device_get_output_name and WL_OUTPUT touch found no matching change.
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/wlroots/wlroots/-/merge_requests?scope=all&state=all&search=libinput_device_get_output_name
Drop this patch when upstream wlroots carries equivalent support.

--- a/backend/libinput/touch.c
+++ b/backend/libinput/touch.c
@@ -1,5 +1,8 @@
 #include <assert.h>
 #include <libinput.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <wlr/util/log.h>
 #include <wlr/interfaces/wlr_touch.h>
 #include "backend/libinput.h"
 
@@ -12,6 +15,14 @@
 	wlr_touch_init(wlr_touch, &libinput_touch_impl, name);
 
+	const char *output = libinput_device_get_output_name(dev->handle);
+	if (output != NULL && output[0] != '\0') {
+		wlr_touch->output_name = strdup(output);
+		if (wlr_touch->output_name == NULL) {
+			wlr_log(WLR_ERROR, "Failed to allocate touch output name");
+		}
+	}
+
 	libinput_device_get_size(dev->handle, &wlr_touch->width_mm,
 		&wlr_touch->height_mm);
 }
